p=2, n=7: checked 64 lifts of 1; every additive order equals 128.
p=2, n=8: checked 128 lifts of 1; every additive order equals 256.
PASS: all finite cyclic calculations.
Scope: these checks illustrate the formula ord(a mod p^n)=p^n when a=1 mod p. The proof of the infinite-product obstruction uses that these orders are unbounded for all n.
